The ModernBERT architecture follows Hugging Face Transformers and ModernBERT.
Runtime tensor operations and Metal attention are provided by Candle.
This project is not an official release of Convai Innovations, Hugging Face,
or the Laya-MLX authors. Downloaded pretrained weights retain their own notices.

src/mlx_gemm_v0322.metal incorporates MLX GPU kernel sources by Apple Inc.,
under the MIT License embedded in that file. The source is pinned to MLX v0.32.2,
revision 1f8e74e3f12f31365464a6867c6579f0e9b29d85:
https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx/tree/1f8e74e3f12f31365464a6867c6579f0e9b29d85/mlx/backend/metal/kernels
Original source paths are preserved as BEGIN comments in the vendored file.
The source is flattened and specialized for this project's Metal dispatch.
Its MIT license is also distributed in LICENSE-MIT.

Rust implementations of Laya architecture, configuration, prompts and calibration
are modified reimplementations for Candle, not unmodified upstream files.
The test checkpoint and golden outputs are synthetic fixtures generated with
upstream Laya; original pretrained model weights are not distributed here.
